              "datalab-163688ca8da9787f5d48edd68d8cc75b_img.jpg": {
                "description": "Figure 7.2.1: First two steps of Kernighan-Lin heuristic for maxcut. The figure shows three bipartite graphs labeled S0, S1, and S2. Each graph has two sets of nodes, A and B on the left, and C and D on the right. Edges connect nodes between the two sets. In S0, edges are (a,A), (a,C), (a,D), (d,A), (d,B), (d,C), (d,D). In S1, edges are (a,A), (a,C), (a,D), (d,A), (d,B), (d,C), (d,D). In S2, edges are (a,A), (a,C), (a,D), (d,A), (d,B), (d,C), (d,D).",
