                "described_at": "2026-06-05T23:25:18",
                "type": "generico",
                "include": true
              },
              "datalab-fc46871d72c65d3381d9201646d23439_img.jpg": {
                "description": "Figure 7.3.2: Two diagrams illustrating vertex assignments. The left diagram shows a circle representing a set of vertices, with a vertex v inside. A solid arrow labeled B_v points from v to a vertex b outside the circle. A dotted arrow labeled A_v points from v to a vertex a below the circle. The right diagram shows a similar circle with two vertices v and pi(v) inside. A solid arrow labeled B_v points from v to a vertex b' above the circle. Another solid arrow labeled B_{pi(v)} points from pi(v) to b'. A dotted arrow labeled A_v points from v to a vertex a below the circle. A solid arrow labeled A_{pi(v)} points from pi(v) to a vertex a' to the right of the circle.",
